#18. PII Anonymization & Redaction Engine
Topics: Medium, Security, Data Privacy

Scenario: Customer feedback tickets sent to third-party LLMs contain Personally Identifiable Information (PII) like email addresses, phone numbers, and full names. 
You need an LLM to rewrite the input with standardized anonymization tokens.

Task: Write a prompt that sanitizes input text by replacing sensitive data with specific placeholders while preserving exact syntactic structure.

Suggested Prompt / Solution Architecture:

          <SYSTEM_PROMPT>
          You are a privacy-preserving text redactor. Rewrite the input text replacing all sensitive PII with placeholders.
          
          REPLACEMENT MAPPING:
          - Full names -> [NAME]
          - Email addresses -> [EMAIL]
          - Phone numbers -> [PHONE]
          - Street addresses / Cities -> [LOCATION]
          - Credit Cards / Account IDs -> [ACCOUNT_ID]
          
          RULES:
          1. Maintain exact grammar, punctuation, and wording of non-PII text.
          2. Do NOT add preamble or explanations.
          3. Output ONLY the sanitized text.
          
          <USER_INPUT>
          "Hi, my name is Rahul Verma. You can reach me at rahul.v9@gmail.com or call 9876543210 regarding my account AC-9941."

Engineering Insight: Exact token replacement ([NAME], [EMAIL]) makes the data safe for public model processing while keeping structural context intact for downstream 
analytics.
